{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291288-which-exalted-is-the-most-sorcerous-feeling-developers","id":1291288,"title":"Which Exalted is the most Sorcerous-feeling? (Developers?)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-23T16:27:36-08:00","id":1291288,"title":"Which Exalted is the most Sorcerous-feeling? (Developers?)","content":"Let me explain myself:<br /> <br /> Solars win conflicts because &quot;I'm supposed to! I'm just that good!&quot; It's kinda what they're built for.<br /> <br /> Lunars win because &quot;I make myself the ideal winner! I pick an animal with the right talents, or a whole bunch of different ones, and suddenly I'm the perfect tool for the job at hand!&quot;<br /> <br /> Sidereals win because &quot;It was meant to be so, because I made sure of it. And you can't prove I did it, so nyah!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> But which of the new Exalted win because &quot;I have rejected the reality that says I lost, and replaced it with one that says I win! Fear my reality-warping powers!&quot; And the reality-warping is blatant, that's key. It's magical. All the sub-divisions of this Exalted have that magical thing about them. Which do I want to play if I'm playing someone who is blatantly playing with supernatural power to win at life?<br /> <br /> EDIT: More on point, their CHARMS feel sorcerous and magical, not just their Sorcery. Their everyday bread + butter Charms <i>also</i> come across as if they're using low-level magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2176,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","user":"SpectacularTentacular","date":". 02-23-2019, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T16:39:23-08:00","id":1291291,"title":"","content":"Probably Infernals","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T16:44:15-08:00","id":1291293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291288-which-exalted-is-the-most-sorcerous-feeling-developers?p=1291291#post1291291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably Infernals</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See, that's kinda what I remember, especially the telekinesis stuff from She Who Lives In Her Name. <i>That's</i> the kinda thing I'm talking about. <br /> <br /> As an aside, I'd love to play an Exalted that threw around TK like Ebony Maw from the Avengers movie. Not sure how I could get that in exalted right now with what we have...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T16:52:17-08:00","id":1291298,"title":"","content":"Getimians are probably going to be a really solid candidate too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T16:56:50-08:00","id":1291300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291288-which-exalted-is-the-most-sorcerous-feeling-developers?p=1291298#post1291298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getimians are probably going to be a really solid candidate too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, what's the lowdown on them? I only have a rough-sketch idea of what they do. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:01:47-08:00","id":1291302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291288-which-exalted-is-the-most-sorcerous-feeling-developers?p=1291300#post1291300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Okay, what's the lowdown on them? I only have a rough-sketch idea of what they do. </div> </div> </div> </div>We know relatively little. They\u2019ll be as Martial Arts geared as the Sidereals, have two types of Essence (Yin and Yang) that cause different effects through their Charms depending on which you spend. Lioness makes a good point, that they\u2019re implied to override Fate to warp reality via their own internal Looms, so they might end up being a fit for what you\u2019re describing, even though they won\u2019t measure up to Infernals and Solars in literal Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:03:36-08:00","id":1291303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291288-which-exalted-is-the-most-sorcerous-feeling-developers?p=1291300#post1291300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Okay, what's the lowdown on them? I only have a rough-sketch idea of what they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anti-sidereals with pattern spiders running down their spines. They will have a yin / yang mote pool with charms that do different things depending on how you pay their cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1174-the-lidless-eye-that-sees","name":"The Lidless Eye That Sees","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1174_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:08:42-08:00","id":1291308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291288-which-exalted-is-the-most-sorcerous-feeling-developers?p=1291300#post1291300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Okay, what's the lowdown on them? I only have a rough-sketch idea of what they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>The previous devs thought sidereals needed a special rival exalt. We don't really have the rules yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:08:44-08:00","id":1291309,"title":"","content":"Hmm. They do sound like a cool night out on the town in their own right. Are they more Terrestrial-level than Celestial, or don't we know enough yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:19:21-08:00","id":1291315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291288-which-exalted-is-the-most-sorcerous-feeling-developers?p=1291309#post1291309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. They do sound like a cool night out on the town in their own right. Are they more Terrestrial-level than Celestial, or don't we know enough yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>As anti-Sidereals they should be on equal footing with Lunars and Sids.<br /> <br /> The Liminals are the new guys on the Terrestrial tier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:23:48-08:00","id":1291317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291288-which-exalted-is-the-most-sorcerous-feeling-developers?p=1291315#post1291315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As anti-Sidereals they should be on equal footing with Lunars and Sids.<br /> <br /> The Liminals are the new guys on the Terrestrial tier.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And...I'm guessing that the Liminals are to the Abyssals what the Getimians are to the Sidereals? Or don't we know yet?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:32:30-08:00","id":1291324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291288-which-exalted-is-the-most-sorcerous-feeling-developers?p=1291317#post1291317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And...I'm guessing that the Liminals are to the Abyssals what the Getimians are to the Sidereals? Or don't we know yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really... they\u2019re both underworld connected but not as inherently adversarial. Liminals are more centered on their own wrestling with what it means to be a human/person/alive than directly at odds with anyone (save of course for how their individual stories unfold). They are gifted exorcists though, so that CAN naturally create conflict with Abyssals expanding shadowlands, summoning ghosts, and otherwise mingling the living and the dead.<br /> <br /> In general though the Liminals are too few in number to have an in-built adversarial relations with beings as powerful as Abyssals (unlike the Dragon-Blooded who can field Legions against their Celestial foes).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:37:39-08:00","id":1291326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291288-which-exalted-is-the-most-sorcerous-feeling-developers?p=1291317#post1291317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And...I'm guessing that the Liminals are to the Abyssals what the Getimians are to the Sidereals? Or don't we know yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Liminals are created when a person denies Creation\u2019s cruelty and attempts to return someone to life once they have passed on. Such attempts never work, but they do allow the Dark Mother to imbue the body with new life, creating a new being with an old body. <br /> <br /> The Dark Mother apparently wishes her children to keep the Underworld and Creation separate, and so they often operate as Ghost Hunters and such things.<br /> <br /> Their role is not directly antagonistic to that of an Abyssal, but it could bring them into conflict. And their creation is entirely unrelated to Abyssals as well.<br /> <br /> Of course there are many Liminals who refuse their role as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T17:43:41-08:00","id":1291330,"title":"","content":"Also, in theory, one could have an Exigent who was Sorcerous and Weird in exactly the way you wanted and there are three more \u201cOptional Exalted\u201d about which we know very little, so they might be options.<br /> <br /> That said, Infernals and Getimians seem to be your best bet at this point. On the other paw, you can make a pretty arcane and creepy Lunar in 3e and we\u2019re only half way through the charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:23:27-08:00","id":1291339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291288-which-exalted-is-the-most-sorcerous-feeling-developers?p=1291330#post1291330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, in theory, one could have an Exigent who was Sorcerous and Weird in exactly the way you wanted and there are three more \u201cOptional Exalted\u201d about which we know very little, so they might be options.<br /> <br /> That said, Infernals and Getimians seem to be your best bet at this point. On the other paw, you can make a pretty arcane and creepy Lunar in 3e and we\u2019re only half way through the charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know what you mean about Lunars, but I'm not gettting the same &quot;sorcerous&quot; vibe I'm talking about from them. They're (<i>to me</i>) more ancient druid and wisecraft due to their use of &quot;all-natural&quot; ingredients. When I think of &quot;sorcerous&quot; I tend to think of a more <i><b>un</b></i>natural vibe. But I agree that you could easily take that to a very Cronenberg-esque level pretty quick. Hell, with the right focus, you could easily do that with a <i>Solar</i> if you wanted. But I'm looking for something unnatural and unsettling right out of the gate that just crackles with scary. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T19:48:11-08:00","id":1291400,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I kind of want to argue against the premises laid out in the original post... mostly on principle, but perhaps on functional grounds of figuring out whether anybody's Charms could fulfil that asked after quality.<br /> <br /> Mind, if it's read literally, I would still imagine that Getimians could actually end up with a lot of Charms consisting of reality substitutions. Infernals maybe, but I feel as though that's more of a high Essence thing for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T20:05:15-08:00","id":1291406,"title":"","content":"Is this a good place to talk about a disconnect between expressing a concept with Dragonblooded versus Solars?<br /> <br /> With Solars, if you want to be a fireball-throwing wizard, you can grab three dots of Occult, jump right into sorcery and spells, and never buy a single Occult Charm.<br /> <br /> With Terrestrials, you can't be a sorcerer without also being a dedicated exorcist, so if you have absolutely in interest in dealing with supernatural creatures with anything more esoteric than a fireball to the face, you actually want to invest in Lore where all of the fireballs are. All of Terrestrial Lore's Charms does a great job of making a Terrestrial feel like a wizard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T20:38:00-08:00","id":1291416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291288-which-exalted-is-the-most-sorcerous-feeling-developers?p=1291330#post1291330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, in theory, one could have an Exigent who was Sorcerous and Weird in exactly the way you wanted and there are <b>three more \u201cOptional Exalted\u201d</b> about which we know very little, so they might be options.<br /> <br /> That said, Infernals and Getimians seem to be your best bet at this point. On the other paw, you can make a pretty arcane and creepy Lunar in 3e and we\u2019re only half way through the charms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are we even still getting those? I somehow got the impression that the ones we were told were totally a thing but had no info on got axed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T21:28:17-08:00","id":1291420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291288-which-exalted-is-the-most-sorcerous-feeling-developers?p=1291416#post1291416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Are we even still getting those? I somehow got the impression that the ones we were told were totally a thing but had no info on got axed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard no deviation from the plan to put the Heart-Eaters, the Umbral Exalted, and the Dream-Souled into an appendix chapter of Exigents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T22:57:15-08:00","id":1291435,"title":"","content":"Cool, glad to hear it more exalts are good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T02:58:29-08:00","id":1291474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291288-which-exalted-is-the-most-sorcerous-feeling-developers?p=1291300#post1291300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, what's the lowdown on them? I only have a rough-sketch idea of what they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're literal walking paradoxes, ripped from the lives they knew and have found themselves manipulated into being part of a Renegade Sidereal's war against Heaven.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T04:03:35-08:00","id":1291488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291288-which-exalted-is-the-most-sorcerous-feeling-developers?p=1291406#post1291406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I<br /> <br /> With Terrestrials, you can't be a sorcerer without also being a dedicated exorcist, so if you have absolutely in interest in dealing with supernatural creatures with anything more esoteric than a fireball to the face, you actually want to invest in Lore where all of the fireballs are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's kind of an illusion. You need four occult charms, and well, there <i>are </i>about four written occult charms at that level, and that's what they do. <br /> <br /> If we get more essence 1 and 2 occult charms this issue will probably vanish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T04:44:39-08:00","id":1291497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291288-which-exalted-is-the-most-sorcerous-feeling-developers#post1291288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars win because &quot;I make myself the ideal winner! I pick an animal with the right talents, or a whole bunch of different ones, and suddenly I'm the perfect tool for the job at hand!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I want to address this one, less for itself, and more because we finally have good Lunar Charms to actually adequately answer the question*.<br /> <br /> That and summarising the Lunar approach solely in terms of their shapeshifting has often sold them a bit short, and has often reasonably fed into concerns with their inadequacy.<br /> <br /> So, with the benefit of previewed Lunar Charms, a more accurate line would be &quot;Lunars win because they can be really good at things in a manner not tied to specific ability, often with an edge of being predatory or tricky or scary or beautiful, unrelenting and unconfinable, and some helpful body mods. Sometimes, they can push how good they are at things a bit further by adopting a complementary animal shape.&quot;<br /> <br /> The problem with phrasing Lunar powers primarily in terms of the benefit of turning into animals is that animals are still mortal, and Lunars are competing at the level of gods and monsters.<br /> <br /> Lunars don't become mighty by turning into animals; animals become mighty because a Lunar turned into them. Protean effects are about that animal body benefiting from becoming a conduit for the Lunar Essence (which can still often get the job done without it). <br /> <br /> * I mean, these punchy one-line summaries of how Exalted do things always tend to be broad to the point of inaccurate, it's just that Lunars have often suffered the worst because their powers besides shapeshifting always felt indistinct in comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T05:47:48-08:00","id":1291506,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. I only wanted to make a distinction between what the Exalts we knew about did and how they did it, and what type of exalted flavor I was looking for. And now I'm interested in the optional Exalts to see what kind of flavoring they have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T06:06:09-08:00","id":1291511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291288-which-exalted-is-the-most-sorcerous-feeling-developers?p=1291488#post1291488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's kind of an illusion. You need four occult charms, and well, there <i>are </i>about four written occult charms at that level, and that's what they do.<br /> <br /> If we get more essence 1 and 2 occult charms this issue will probably vanish.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so, because Occult is by definition the Ability for dealing with supernatural creatures in esoteric ways other than punching them in the face. Solar Occult Charms represent being an exorcist just as much as Terrestrial Occult Charms.<br /> <br /> The difference is that the Dragon-Blood actually needs to invest into that archetype to access sorcery, where the Solar can pay lipservice to it; meanwhile the Dragon-Blood doesn't need sorcery at all to be a fireball wizard, where a Solar does.<br /> <br /> The difference is enough to change whether I would have a character favor Lore or Occult depending on if they're a Dragon-Blood or a Solar.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that any of this is BAD, mind you. But it certainly is quirky.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lunars don't have this issue partially because they don't favor Abilities in the first place, but mostly because &quot;any five Mental Attribute Charms&quot; is not nearly as definitive as &quot;four or five Terrestrial Occult Charms&quot;. A Lunar could buy up the Intelligence Warfare Charms and be a fireball wizard who is also a general. Or a fireball wizard who is also a crafter, or a healer.<br /> <br /> Technically, I'm not sure a Lunar even needs to have any dots in Occult to be a sorcerer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 02-24-2019, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T09:11:02-08:00","id":1291546,"title":"","content":"Dragon-Blooded didn\u2019t even make the list of exalted. <br /> <br /> /sadface","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T10:40:57-08:00","id":1291560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291288-which-exalted-is-the-most-sorcerous-feeling-developers?p=1291506#post1291506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. I only wanted to make a distinction between what the Exalts we knew about did and how they did it, and what type of exalted flavor I was looking for. And now I'm interested in the optional Exalts to see what kind of flavoring they have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vance just answered a question about one of them. They might be the one you want to watch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1291378#post1291378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Dream-Souled, one of the &amp;quot;optional canon&amp;quot; Exalted that will be presented in the appendix to <i>Exigents</i>, are Chosen by a thing of the Wyld, but the consequences of their actions are as inimical to the raksha as they are to Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}